stream
BT 0.42 0.45 0.44 rg /F1 7 Tf 525.1 30 Td (Page 1) Tj ET
0.93 0.95 0.94 rg 0 731.89 595.28 110 re f
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F2 22 Tf 48 789.89 Td (What inspectors ask staff) Tj ET
BT 0.3 0.33 0.32 rg /F1 11 Tf 48 763.89 Td (The questions care staff get asked on the day, and what a good answer contains.) Tj ET
BT 0.05 0.36 0.27 rg /F2 11 Tf 496.56 795.89 Td (Staffbook) Tj ET
BT 0.42 0.45 0.44 rg /F1 8 Tf 443.22 779.89 Td (Free to keep, copy and share) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10.5 Tf 48 701.89 Td (Under the inspection framework, inspectors speak to staff alone, permanent and agency, so people can) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10.5 Tf 48 686.89 Td (say what they think. They also sit in on handover and watch how staff and children talk to each other. There) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10.5 Tf 48 671.89 Td (is no script and there should not be one: a home that runs well does not need rehearsed answers. This) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10.5 Tf 48 656.89 Td (page exists so nobody is surprised by the question.) Tj ET
BT 0.42 0.45 0.44 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 48 636.89 Td (The framework's own words on what it looks for: staff are "clear about, and follow, procedures for responding to) Tj ET
BT 0.42 0.45 0.44 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 48 623.39 Td (concerns about the safety of a child"; children who go missing get a "well-coordinated" response; restraint is "used only) Tj ET
BT 0.42 0.45 0.44 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 48 609.89 Td (when necessary" and every incident is "recorded, reviewed and monitored by leaders"; staff use "effective) Tj ET
BT 0.42 0.45 0.44 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 48 596.39 Td (de-escalation techniques"; supervision is "regular and effective" and "focused on children's experiences".) Tj ET
BT 0.05 0.36 0.27 rg /F2 11 Tf 48 571.89 Td ("How would you report a concern about a child's safety?") Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 58 553.89 Td (The steps in order, with names: your manager, the designated officer \(LADO\) and their number, who covers) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 58 539.89 Td (out of hours, and that you would write it down the same day. If the concern is about the manager, who then.) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 58 525.89 Td (Hesitation on the names is the usual gap.) Tj ET
BT 0.05 0.36 0.27 rg /F2 11 Tf 48 500.89 Td ("What do you do if a child goes missing?") Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 58 482.89 Td (That child's own missing plan, not a generic one: when the police are called, who else is told \(social worker,) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 58 468.89 Td (parents if the plan says so\), what you do while they are gone, and the return home interview afterwards.) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 58 454.89 Td (Where the plan lives.) Tj ET
BT 0.05 0.36 0.27 rg /F2 11 Tf 48 429.89 Td ("When can you use physical restraint, and what happens after?") Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 58 411.89 Td (Only to prevent injury or serious harm, only the holds you are trained in, never as a punishment. Afterwards:) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 58 397.89 Td (the record the same day, the child's view and yours, the manager's review, the debrief. If you are not yet) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 58 383.89 Td (trained, say so and say what you do instead.) Tj ET
BT 0.05 0.36 0.27 rg /F2 11 Tf 48 358.89 Td ("Tell me about the plan for a child you know well.") Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 58 340.89 Td (Their needs and risks, what the plan asks staff to do, what is working and what is not, and what the child says) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 58 326.89 Td (about it. Inspectors then open the file and look for the same story.) Tj ET
BT 0.05 0.36 0.27 rg /F2 11 Tf 48 301.89 Td ("What would you do if you saw a colleague do something wrong?") Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 58 283.89 Td (The whistleblowing route, and that you can go outside the home: the Responsible Individual, the LADO,) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 58 269.89 Td (Ofsted. That you would not need permission, and would not be treated worse for it.) Tj ET
BT 0.05 0.36 0.27 rg /F2 11 Tf 48 244.89 Td ("How do you know what has happened to each child before your shift?") Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 58 226.89 Td (Handover, the daily logs, the plan updates. Inspectors watch a handover, so this answer gets checked against) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 58 212.89 Td (what they see.) Tj ET
BT 0.05 0.36 0.27 rg /F2 11 Tf 48 187.89 Td ("What training have you had, and what is next?") Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 58 169.89 Td (Your mandatory courses and whether they are in date, where you are with the level 3, and something you) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 58 155.89 Td (asked for. "I don't know when my first aid runs out" is the answer to avoid, and the training matrix is how you) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 58 141.89 Td (avoid it.) Tj ET
BT 0.05 0.36 0.27 rg /F2 11 Tf 48 116.89 Td ("How often are you supervised, and is it any use?") Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 58 98.89 Td (The cycle \(every four to six weeks is common\), the last date, and an honest view. Supervision that is "a date) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 58 84.89 Td (and two signatures" is a finding; saying so is not.) Tj ET
